From: Tao Gong <gongtao0607@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: mt7530: trap frames to the conduit on EN7581 and AN7583

Frames trapped by the switch only reach the CPU when MT7530_CPU_EN and
MT7530_CPU_PORT are set in MT753X_MFC. EN7581 and AN7583 only set the CPU
port bitmap in MT7531_CFC and are skipped by mt753x_conduit_state_change(),
so BPDUs and LLDP frames from switch user ports are dropped.

Program the MFC CPU port bits for both SoCs as well.

Signed-off-by: Tao Gong <gongtao0607@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/mt7530.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/mt7530.c
@@ -3333,7 +3333,8 @@
 	 * interface is up.
 	 */
 	if (priv->id != ID_MT7530 && priv->id != ID_MT7621 &&
-	    priv->id != ID_EN7528)
+	    priv->id != ID_EN7528 && priv->id != ID_EN7581 &&
+	    priv->id != ID_AN7583)
 		return;
 
 	mask = BIT(cpu_dp->index);
